  data:  # 0e78
    kind: work_item  # 0e78
    title: "Sketch quotes files that git ignores and does not track (a stray local output file appears in the Configuration section): discovery has no rule for ignored-and-untracked files"  # 0e78
    status: needs_human_review  # 0e78
    priority: 3  # 0e78
    parent:  # 0e78
    tags:  # 0e78
    - outside_reader_review_20261113  # 0e78
    - dogfood  # 0e78
    - sketch  # 0e78
    - discovery  # 0e78
    isbefore: []  # 0e78
    duplicate_of: []  # 0e78
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 0e78
    pr_ref:  # 0e78
    description: "Source: an outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/49869475df136c86/eb6b68753d44e259. Every claim below was re-checked against those files and the code on dev 847ce5888e.\n\nOBSERVED. Every sketch of this repository carries, under Configuration, \"[packages/hypergumbo-core/slice.json]\" with an entry node \"python:src/main.py:1-2:my_func:function\". That file is a leftover local output from July: git check-ignore reports it ignored by .gitignore line 22 (slice.json), and git ls-files does not list it. A reader takes it for part of the project.\n\nMECHANISM. sketch._discover_config_files_embedding (and the other sketch file walks) take their files from discovery's FileIndex or from rglob. Discovery consults git in two places only, both for DIRECTORIES (ADR-0004 point 7: dist/build/out beside a package.json when positively untracked; a self-ignoring .gitignore when the directory is not committed). Nothing asks whether a single FILE is ignored and untracked. ADR-0004 point 3 rules the converse case (a tracked file is real even where the name looks derived); the record is silent on this one.\n\nWHAT NEEDS DECIDING (the record is silent, so this is a ruling for the owner before code)\n- Is a file that the repository's VCS ignores AND does not track part of what hypergumbo describes? Arguments for \"no\": it is by the project's own declaration not project content (local outputs, editor state, secrets files, caches), and quoting it in a sketch misleads; the analysis of a clean checkout and of a working tree would then agree. Arguments for \"yes\" or \"not everywhere\": a non-git directory has no such signal, so behaviour would differ by VCS; some teams ignore generated-but-meaningful files; excluding by ignore rules from ANALYSIS is a larger change than excluding from what the sketch QUOTES.\n- If \"no\": at which layer. Options: (a) discovery, for every consumer (analysis, sketch, verify-claims); (b) the sketch's quoting sections only (Configuration, Additional Files, Source Files Content); (c) disclosure only: keep the file and mark it \"untracked, ignored\".\n- How the answer is obtained cheaply and correctly: one git call per run listing ignored-untracked paths (git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard), cached with the file index; nothing when the directory is not a git work tree.\n\nMEASURE BEFORE CHOOSING. On this checkout and on at least three other working trees, how many discovered files are ignored-and-untracked, of what kinds, and how many of them reach a node, a Configuration quote or an Additional Files entry today.\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was seen. A fix keyed to this repo's paths or file names, or one that works only for Python, does not close this item.\nThe rule must be stated in terms of the VCS's own answer, never a list of names such as slice.json; it must say what happens with no VCS, and with a VCS other than git if one is detected. Secrets files (.env) are the case to get right: they are commonly ignored, and a sketch that quotes one is worse than a sketch that quotes a stale output."  # 0e78
    fields: {}  # 0e78
- op: discuss  # 36e4
  at: '2026-11-13T22:18:38Z'  # 36e4
  by: agent  # 36e4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 36e4
  clock: 2  # 36e4
  nonce: '36e4'  # 36e4
  message: "MEASURED 2026-11-13 (the item's \"MEASURE BEFORE CHOOSING\"); no code changed, the layer is still yours to rule. Scripts and results: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jolov_ignored_untracked_11132026 (RESULTS.md).\n\n1. HOW COMMON. 580 git work trees among the local clones; 23 have a file git ignores and does not track, 10 after removing duplicate clones. The other 557 are fresh clones nobody built in.\n\n2. WHAT DISCOVERY ALREADY DROPS. Over those 10 trees, 107,754 ignored-and-untracked files; discovery's FileIndex holds 97 of them (99.9% are already left out by the dependency, build-output and cache rules). Seven trees have 0 left (Rust target/, Python __pycache__). The three with a residue: this checkout 31 (16 slice outputs, 7 run logs under .ci/, slice.json, two fixture package.json, .env, AUTONOMOUS_MODE.txt); thc_dev 3 (.env.dev and two .pem files, one a private key); thc_prod 63 (.env and 62 built static assets). So the residue is small and is the two kinds the item names: local outputs and secrets.\n\n3. WHAT REACHES THE GRAPH AND THE SKETCH HERE. 19 of this checkout's 31 have a node in the survey (19 file nodes, plus 2 package and 2 dependency nodes from the fixture package.json). packages/hypergumbo-core/slice.json is quoted under Configuration at 8k and listed under Additional Files at 128k. A sketch of `git archive HEAD` has none of the 31: a working tree and a clean checkout of one commit give different sketches. The thc trees were not sketched, because their residue is real secrets.\n\n4. THE SECRETS CASE, on a synthetic repository (3 tracked files, 13 ignored-and-untracked files each holding a fake value; fixture_repo/ in the notebook directory). `hypergumbo sketch . -t 8000` prints, in full, under Additional Files Content: config/secrets.yml, credentials.json, terraform.tfvars, settings.local.toml, local.json, notes.md, out/result.json. All 7 at 8k and 32k; 5 of them at 2k, config/secrets.yml and credentials.json included. Not printed: .env, .env.dev, .env.local, .npmrc, id_rsa, server_key.pem. Those six are left out because of their file type (dotfile, no recognised extension, .pem). Neither sketch.py nor discovery.py has any rule about ignored files or secrets.\n\nWHAT THIS SAYS ABOUT THE OPTIONS\n(a) discovery, for every consumer: closes section 4 and also removes the 19 node-bearing files from the graph. One `git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard` per run: 0.04 s on wasmtime (7,558 paths), 0.12 s here (60,133).\n(b) the sketch's quoting sections only: closes section 4, leaves the graph as it is.\n(c) disclosure only: leaves section 4 open.\n\nMY RECOMMENDATION: (a), and I would raise this above P3, because a sketch is made to be pasted into a model and today it can carry a credentials file. Priority is yours to change; I have not changed it. Not measured: a VCS other than git; a directory with no VCS (no signal exists there); submodules and nested work trees."  # 36e4
